413
00:24:25,161 --> 00:24:26,660
It wasn't green.

414
00:24:26,760 --> 00:24:27,960
The wind blew.

415
00:24:28,060 --> 00:24:29,260
It was cold.

416
00:24:29,360 --> 00:24:31,860
And when the wind blew, the sand blew.

417
00:24:31,960 --> 00:24:36,700
And the dorms weren't built that tight.

418
00:24:36,800 --> 00:24:41,100
And consequently, the sand went through.

419
00:24:41,200 --> 00:24:43,820
You could have a hanger closed up,

420
00:24:43,920 --> 00:24:47,380
and it would be enough sand that would seep in through the

421
00:24:47,480 --> 00:24:50,760
crevices whereby they could take a truckload of sand out

422
00:24:50,860 --> 00:24:55,160
of that hanger after about three days of high winds.

423
00:24:55,161 --> 00:24:58,300
The sand and wind were a constant problem.

424
00:24:58,400 --> 00:25:01,400
But as progress continued at Edwards, both the accommodations

425
00:25:01,500 --> 00:25:06,600
and the aircraft got better. In the late 50s, the Air Force

426
00:25:06,700 --> 00:25:10,000
flight testers and their civilian counterparts at the NACA,

